<task id="042" project="email-communication-solution-r5">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-02 / NFR-07: Standalone Email code page `src/solutions/EmailPage/**` (`main.tsx` + ADR-028 auth bootstrap)</title>
    <phase>4 Dual-use surface</phase>
    <gate>after:040</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New code-page surface with an auth bootstrap (ADR-028) and fail-closed authorization; tags include auth + code-page + `.tsx`. The unauthenticated/fail-closed path is non-negotiable. FULL gate.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Copy of the established `DailyBriefing`/`EventsPage` code-page mount + auth bootstrap; low ambiguity, exact reference to mirror. Sonnet @ high.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P4</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>New `src/solutions/EmailPage/**` tree — disjoint from the widget-mount files (041). Both depend only on 040; no shared-file write.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>040</deps>
    <tags>frontend, code-page, auth</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Create the standalone Email code page `src/solutions/EmailPage/**` — its own `main.tsx` + ADR-028 auth bootstrap — reachable from Spaarke navigation, that renders the SHARED `EmailWorkspace` component (040) in React 19 (FR-02, mount #2 of Pattern D). Copy the `DailyBriefing` mount pattern (`src/solutions/DailyBriefing/src/main.tsx`): `createRoot` + host `FluentProvider` (theme via `resolveCodePageTheme`/`setupCodePageThemeListener`) + `AppErrorBoundary` + async `bootstrapAuth` (`resolveRuntimeConfig` → `ensureAuthInitialized`). Reuse `@spaarke/auth` `authenticatedFetch` for the `.eml` render call — no new auth surface (NFR-07). The page MUST fail closed when unauthenticated.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Spaarke React 19 Code Pages + ADR-028 Auth v2 bootstrap (`@spaarke/auth`) + Vite build. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>A new `src/solutions/EmailPage/` Vite React 19 code page with `src/main.tsx` (mirroring `DailyBriefing/src/main.tsx`) that: bootstraps auth via `@spaarke/auth` (`resolveRuntimeConfig` + `ensureAuthInitialized`), owns the host `FluentProvider` (light/dark via `resolveCodePageTheme`), wraps in `AppErrorBoundary`, and renders the shared `EmailWorkspace` from `@spaarke/communication-components` — supplying an `authenticatedFetch` for the `.eml` render call. The page is registered as a Spaarke navigation-reachable web resource. Unauthenticated access fails closed (auth bootstrap gates the surface; the `.eml`/data calls 401 and surface an error state, never raw content).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-02 + NFR-07 + design Lens 2: mount #2 of the dual-use surface is a standalone Email code page with its own `main.tsx` + auth bootstrap (the `DailyBriefing`/`EventsPage` pattern), reachable from Spaarke navigation, rendering the SAME shared `EmailWorkspace` component so both mounts render identically (dual-mount parity, NFR-06). `DailyBriefing/src/main.tsx` is the exact reference: `createRoot`, `FluentProvider` with `resolveCodePageTheme`, `AppErrorBoundary`, and an async non-blocking `bootstrapAuth()` calling `resolveRuntimeConfig()` + `ensureAuthInitialized()` from `@spaarke/auth`.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/solutions/EmailPage/src/main.tsx</file>
      <file role="new">src/solutions/EmailPage/src/config/runtimeConfig.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/solutions/EmailPage/src/services/authInit.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/solutions/EmailPage/package.json</file>
      <file role="new">src/solutions/EmailPage/vite.config.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/solutions/EmailPage/index.html</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/DailyBriefing/src/main.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/DailyBriefing/src/services/authInit.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="040" status="pending">The shared `EmailWorkspace` component this page renders.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Auth bootstrap MUST reuse `@spaarke/auth` (`resolveRuntimeConfig` → `ensureAuthInitialized`, `getAuthProvider`) — NO new auth surface, NO token snapshots (NFR-07). All BFF calls (the `.eml` render) go through `@spaarke/auth` `authenticatedFetch`. The surface MUST fail closed: without a resolved auth context the data/`.eml` calls 401 and the pane shows an error state — never renders unauthorized content.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">The code page owns the host `FluentProvider` with `resolveCodePageTheme` + `setupCodePageThemeListener` (light/dark). The shared `EmailWorkspace` inherits this theme (it mounts no `FluentProvider` of its own).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">React 19 code page. MUST NOT introduce an `as React.ComponentType` cast on this new code-page work (NFR-05). Renders the shared component directly.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Render the SHARED `EmailWorkspace` (040) — MUST NOT fork or re-implement the surface; the code page is a thin mount + auth bootstrap. The shared lib stays Xrm/host-agnostic (host-specific thunks like `navigateTo` are supplied from here).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Vite install/build: `npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund`; build via `npm run build` (Vite code page, NOT a PCF build).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Spaarke React 19 code-page mount + ADR-028 auth bootstrap</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-006-pcf-vs-codepage.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-v9-adoption.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/auth/spaarke-sso-binding.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/auth-deployment-setup.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Code-page mount + auth bootstrap" location="src/solutions/DailyBriefing/src/main.tsx">`createRoot` + `FluentProvider theme={resolveCodePageTheme()}` + `AppErrorBoundary` + async `bootstrapAuth()` (`resolveRuntimeConfig`→`setRuntimeConfig`→`ensureAuthInitialized`→tenant resolve). Copy this shape; render `EmailWorkspace` in place of `DailyBriefingApp`.</pattern>
      <pattern name="authenticatedFetch" location="@spaarke/auth">Supply `authenticatedFetch` to `EmailWorkspace` for the `GET /api/documents/{id}/eml-render` call — no token handled in page code.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load spec FR-02/NFR-07 + ADR-028 + the `DailyBriefing` reference. Declare RIGOR LEVEL: FULL with reason. Confirm 040 is ✅ (the `EmailWorkspace` export exists).</step>
    <step order="1">Scaffold `src/solutions/EmailPage/` (package.json, vite.config.ts, index.html, tsconfig) mirroring `DailyBriefing`'s solution shape; install with `npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund`.</step>
    <step order="2">Author `src/main.tsx` copying `DailyBriefing/src/main.tsx`: `createRoot`, host `FluentProvider` with `resolveCodePageTheme` + `setupCodePageThemeListener`, `AppErrorBoundary surfaceName="Email"`, async non-blocking `bootstrapAuth()` (`resolveRuntimeConfig` → `setRuntimeConfig` → `ensureAuthInitialized` → tenant resolve).</step>
    <step order="3">Render the shared `EmailWorkspace` from `@spaarke/communication-components`, passing an `authenticatedFetch` (from `@spaarke/auth`) for the `.eml` render call and the Dataverse data adapter (`Xrm.WebApi` shim / `IDataverseClient`) supplied by the host.</step>
    <step order="4">Add config/runtimeConfig.ts + services/authInit.ts mirroring the DailyBriefing equivalents so `bootstrapAuth` resolves runtime config + MSAL.</step>
    <step order="5">Register the page as a Spaarke navigation-reachable web resource (sitemap/nav entry) following the existing code-page navigation convention.</step>
    <step order="6">Build the page (`npm run build`); render locally and verify: authenticated → surface renders; simulate unauthenticated (no auth context) → data/`.eml` calls 401 → error state (fail closed), no unauthorized content. Verify no `as React.ComponentType` cast (NFR-05).</step>
    <step order="7">Update `projects/email-communication-solution-r5/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set 042 to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document the code-page build output + navigation registration + the `EmailWorkspaceProps` supplied here in `projects/email-communication-solution-r5/notes/` for the deploy task 051.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the standalone code-page host cannot supply the same data adapter contract `EmailWorkspace` expects (from 040) without a code-page-specific fork, OR if fail-closed authorization cannot be guaranteed through `@spaarke/auth` alone, STOP and escalate per root CLAUDE.md §6 rather than adding a new auth surface or diverging the shared component.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>`src/solutions/DailyBriefing/` and `src/solutions/EventsPage/` — existing standalone code pages with the same mount + auth-bootstrap pattern; `communications-list` widget is the SpaarkeAi-hosted surface.</existing>
    <extension>No — those are different surfaces (daily briefing / events); the Email mailbox is a distinct standalone destination reachable from Spaarke navigation. It reuses the mount + auth-bootstrap pattern (copied, not forked) and renders the shared `EmailWorkspace`.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without a standalone `EmailPage`, the shared `EmailWorkspace` has no code-page mount — the standalone-destination half of the dual-use Pattern D (FR-02) is missing, and users have no full-screen mailbox reachable from Spaarke navigation (Success Criterion 1 "opens as a standalone code page" fails).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Standalone page loads + authenticates + renders">
      <steps><step>Open the Email code page as an authenticated user.</step><step>Wait for auth bootstrap.</step></steps>
      <expected>The shared `EmailWorkspace` two-pane surface renders; `.eml` render calls go through `authenticatedFetch`; the page matches the widget mount (dual-mount parity).</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Unauthenticated fails closed (negative)">
      <steps><step>Open the page with no resolvable auth context.</step></steps>
      <expected>Data/`.eml` calls 401; the pane shows an error/retry state — no email content is rendered (fails closed).</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark-mode render (ADR-021)">
      <steps><step>Set the host theme to dark and open the page.</step></steps>
      <expected>The code page's `FluentProvider` applies the dark theme; the Email surface renders legibly; no React-version cast on the mount (NFR-05).</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools><tool name="npm">Install (`--legacy-peer-deps`) + build the Vite code page</tool><tool name="terminal">shell</tool></tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/EmailPage/src/main.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/EmailPage/src/services/authInit.ts</output>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/EmailPage/package.json</output>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/EmailPage/vite.config.ts</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an authenticated user, when the Email code page loads, then auth bootstraps via `@spaarke/auth` (`resolveRuntimeConfig` + `ensureAuthInitialized`) and the shared `EmailWorkspace` surface renders.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the code page, when it issues the `.eml` render request, then it uses `@spaarke/auth` `authenticatedFetch` — no new auth surface, no token handled in page code (NFR-07).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the rendered page, when compared with the widget mount (041), then the surface is identical (dual-mount parity via the shared component).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (fail closed): given no resolvable auth context, when the page loads, then the data/`.eml` calls return 401 and the pane shows an error state — no unauthorized email content is rendered.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (NFR-05): the mount introduces no `as React.ComponentType` cast and imports no PCF `ComponentFramework` type.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The page renders legibly in dark mode via its own `FluentProvider` (ADR-021 dark-mode ui-test passes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The page is reachable from Spaarke navigation (web-resource/nav entry registered); the Vite build is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Reference spec FR-02 + NFR-07 + design Lens 2. Copy `DailyBriefing/src/main.tsx` mount + auth bootstrap. Render the shared `EmailWorkspace` (040) — do not fork. Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (imports `@spaarke/communication-components`). Completion summary appended here when done.</notes>

